swer/id #uuid "4dfeae96-2ba1-52c2-bf4c-472193de0ecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195210} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f089bd-0d93-5349-8b77-6eb575868fde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c28df386-4e37-5537-beaf-35f25b2c6e2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-181269" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/assets/f00499aad7b915267fe99bde8c13665a325cf6409e2e856466e9cdc90e4a8b8a.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,2x-3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=2x-3.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<2x-3\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=2x-3$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x-3\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 2x-3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79a183d8-de28-59a3-9974-d37d48fdd352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368779} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a9200f-7a2b-5ae0-b60d-957a7fe4c521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value